        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ec6166de-973c-503e-8da9-f6de8c524df5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Norman Z. McLeod, Sam Wanamaker, Cy Endfield, Wallace Beery, Marjorie Main, Mandy Miller, André Morell\n- Works: Jackass Mail, The Secret\n- Roles: film directors, actors, writers, cartoonists\n- Topics: American film, British film, Hollywood blacklist\n\nFacts:\n- Norman Zenos McLeod was born on September 20, 1898, and he was an American film director, cartoonist, and writer.\n- Sam Wanamaker was born as Samuel Wattenmacker on June 14, 1919, and he later became an American actor and director.\n- In 1942, Jackass Mail was released as a Western comedy film directed by Norman Z. McLeod and starring Wallace Beery and Marjorie Main.\n- In 1955, The Secret was released as a British crime drama directed by Cy Endfield and starring Sam Wanamaker, Mandy Miller, and André Morell.\n- Sam Wanamaker moved to the United Kingdom after he feared being blacklisted in Hollywood because of his early pronounced liberal sympathies.\n- Norman Z. McLeod died on January 27, 1964.\n- Sam Wanamaker was appointed CBE, and he died on December 18, 1993.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
